<h2>How calls are kept safe</h2>
<p>We call the influencer first and announce that you want to talk. The influencer chooses whether to accept before you are dialled. Both calls come from a platform number, so your private number and the influencer's stay hidden. Either person can hang up at any time; pressing <strong>#</strong> ends the call and blocks the other person.</p>
<p>You can report and block anyone, and after our team reviews a report, serious or repeated violations lead to strikes and bans. Watch out for scams: anyone who asks you for an OTP, UPI PIN, password, card or bank details is a scammer. The platform never asks for them. No human monitors or listens to your calls. Talking about distress is never a reason for a strike.</p>
<p>You do not owe anyone your number, identity documents, money, private contact or another minute of conversation. Leave if you feel uncomfortable. The <a href="/women-only">women's safety guide</a> explains Women-only channels, boundaries and respectful discussion of women's experiences. Most questions are answered in the <a href="/faq">FAQs</a>.</p>
